      ],
      bestUses: ['Wheelbarrows and garden carts', 'Push and riding mowers', 'Zero-turn mowers', 'ATVs and compact equipment'],
      planning: ['Use the machine’s actual width and operating weight', 'Low mower decks need a gentle transition', 'Traction for wet and frosty days'],
      prices: prices.ramps.equipment,
    },
    {
      id: 'steps-landings',
      name: 'Entry Steps & Landings',
      intro: [
        'A house-style door, office or studio entrance usually needs steps rather than a ramp. A landing gives a stable place to stand while opening the door instead of balancing on a stair tread.',
      ],
      prices: prices.ramps.steps,
    },
    {
      id: 'composite',
      name: 'Composite & Premium Access',
      intro: [
        'Composite decking reduces surface upkeep and looks more finished at high-visibility entries. The frame underneath is still structural, and composite boards are checked for traction, since not all behave the same on a wet or frosty slope.',
      ],
      bestUses: ['Backyard offices and studios', 'Pool houses', 'Premium retreats', 'Porch-integrated buildings'],
      prices: prices.ramps.premium,
    },
    {
      id: 'mobility',
      name: 'Mobility-Oriented Ramps',
      intro: [
        'Convenience access and accessibility access are not the same. A ramp meant for mobility use can need much more length, landings, handrails, edge protection and yard space than a mower ramp.',
        'Appalachian Sheds does not describe a ramp as ADA compliant unless the complete project has been designed and verified to the applicable standard for your location.',
      ],
      prices: prices.ramps.mobility,
    },
    {
      id: 'concrete',
      name: 'Concrete & Permanent Approaches',
      intro: [
        'Concrete gives a durable, permanent approach for frequent equipment traffic or when the entry joins a walk or patio. It is less forgiving than wood if the floor height or drainage is wrong, so it is poured after those are final.',
      ],
      prices: prices.ramps.concrete,
    },
  ],
  compare: {
    title: 'Choose Access by Use',
    head: ['Primary use', 'Recommended access', 'Planning range'],
    rows: [
      ['Garden and light storage', 'Standard PT ramp or low transition', '$450–$900'],
      ['Riding mower', 'Wide PT equipment ramp', '$650–$1,100'],
      ['Zero-turn, ATV or heavy equipment', 'Reinforced equipment ramp', '$850–$1,700+'],
      ['Walk-in entry', 'Steps, or steps with a landing', '$650–$1,600+'],
      ['Premium office or studio', 'Finished landing, composite ramp or architectural steps', '$950–$3,000+'],
      ['Mobility-oriented access', 'Longer ramp system with code review', '$1,500–$6,000+'],
      ['Permanent equipment approach', 'Concrete system', '$1,500–$4,500+'],
    ],
  },
  considerationsTitle: 'Plan the Door, Floor Height and Ramp Together',
  considerations: [
    ['Door width', 'Size the ramp to the clear opening and the widest item you will move.'],
