    ['Drainage', 'The approach should shed water away from the door and the building pad.'],
  ],
  faqs: [
    { q: 'How much does a shed ramp cost?', a: 'A site-built pressure-treated garden-cart ramp is $450 to $750, a riding-mower ramp $650 to $1,100, and a zero-turn ramp $850 to $1,400 or more.' },
    { q: 'Why does a site-built ramp cost more than a factory ramp?', a: 'Factory ramps are short, standard accessories. A site-built ramp is fitted to your actual floor height, door width, equipment and approach, and set on a stable base.' },
    { q: 'Is the ramp ADA compliant?', a: 'Not by default. A ramp is described as accessible only when the full project has been designed and verified to the applicable standard for your location.' },
  ],
  ctaTitle: 'Plan Your Entry With Edwin',
};
---
<OptionPage page={page} />
